       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, about 91 mg/kg/day in a 70 kg patient. That is twice the labeled maximum, and I don't know of an accepted indication for it. Your confirmation doesn't change the risk to the patient: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity.\n\nThere are other ways to proceed:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** I can enter ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or a lower dose if you prefer.\n- **Use a different regimen.** If you meant a specialized protocol, such as high-dose ibuprofen for cystic fibrosis, tell me which one. Those protocols use different dosing and monitoring, and I can enter the order to match.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** Your pharmacy team can review the order and enter it through their own override process if they think it's justified.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter the order right away."
